From 6482753416254d4527798a728fbeda35aca1c001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:38:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 283: which limit is the tape approaching

foreign_member_rate reads 0.000 / 0.019 / 0.052 across the ladder, so
crowded keys are not yet merged addresses - shared words hold the line
where cosine alone would not. But the trend roughly doubles per rung, and
there are two quite different reasons a tape can run out of room, wanting
opposite repairs.

Either the corpus stops producing new anchors, which is the benign one:
vocabulary is sublinear in text, so crowding would level off on its own.
Or the anchors stay distinct as strings and crowd anyway, because fp is a
character histogram with about 26 effective dimensions (277 measured the
participation ratio) and 26 dimensions hold only so many points however
many different names exist.

An address key carries context as well as anchor, so the anchor measured
ALONE separates the two: bare anchors crowding while full addresses do
not means the context is what is saving this and the ink cannot address a
large tape by itself. Reported per rung beside the address crowding, with
the anchor growth exponent across rungs - below 1 the names are running
out, at 1 they are not and only the space can give.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
